WEBVTT

00:00:06.990 --> 00:00:13.250
Romeo's Blue Skies

00:00:08.210 --> 00:00:13.250
"To the Sky..."

00:00:13.590 --> 00:00:17.890
<i>Overlooking the rows of houses and stores</i>

00:00:18.310 --> 00:00:22.300
<i>from the highest vantage,</i>

00:00:22.960 --> 00:00:27.410
<i>Such things as tears and sadness</i>

00:00:27.480 --> 00:00:31.550
<i>will quickly vanish</i>

00:00:32.770 --> 00:00:37.110
<i>The birds, wind, and sunshine...</i>

00:00:37.440 --> 00:00:41.300
<i>...all are your friends</i>

00:00:41.710 --> 00:00:46.370
<i>I'll carry this dream farther than far</i>

00:00:46.410 --> 00:00:51.460
<i>...no matter the distance...</i>

00:00:53.130 --> 00:00:58.220
<i>I long to fly freely</i>

00:00:58.550 --> 00:01:02.500
<i>through the blue sky in my heart...</i>

00:01:02.540 --> 00:01:05.430
<i>The far distant blue sky</i>

00:01:05.540 --> 00:01:12.880
<i>It flows into tomorrow</i>

00:01:19.020 --> 00:01:25.220
Takara Fansubs

00:01:28.100 --> 00:01:33.240
<i>Romeo worked hard to go to the circus with his friends.</i>

00:01:35.600 --> 00:01:42.380
<i>But the money was used to pay for a keepsake from Michaelo's mother.</i>

00:01:43.600 --> 00:01:47.930
<i>The bonds uniting the boys grew stronger.</i>

00:01:48.330 --> 00:01:53.330
Episode 32:

00:01:48.330 --> 00:01:53.330
A Lovely Christmas Eve

00:01:54.660 --> 00:01:58.370
<i>Christmas was approaching in Milan.</i>

00:01:59.020 --> 00:02:06.470
<i>A serenity befitting the holy day descended on this bustling town.</i>

00:02:19.410 --> 00:02:21.870
It's almost Christmas...

00:02:24.940 --> 00:02:28.670
Soon everybody will be on vacation to celebrate with their family.

00:02:32.220 --> 00:02:33.840
What's wrong, Romeo?

00:02:34.380 --> 00:02:37.090
We've got three more buildings left today.

00:02:37.420 --> 00:02:39.780
I'll be just another minute.

00:02:42.590 --> 00:02:43.750
Romeo!

00:02:47.150 --> 00:02:49.110
Are you okay, Romeo?

00:02:49.130 --> 00:02:50.540
I'm fine.

00:02:52.000 --> 00:02:54.750
Don't move. Your leg is broken.

00:02:54.770 --> 00:02:56.420
My leg is broken??

00:02:57.070 --> 00:02:59.800
It's best that you don't move for a while.

00:02:59.990 --> 00:03:03.070
I've spoken to your boss about this...

00:03:03.430 --> 00:03:08.180
Romeo, the doctor has kindly offered to let you stay with him.

00:03:08.190 --> 00:03:10.420
But I've got work to...

00:03:10.440 --> 00:03:14.620
I wouldn't make an injured person work. I'm not that low.

00:03:14.630 --> 00:03:17.510
Take your time recuperating here at my house.

00:03:17.780 --> 00:03:19.340
You'll even have a little nurse.

00:03:20.890 --> 00:03:24.260
Romeo... we'll be spending Christmas Day here.

00:03:24.500 --> 00:03:27.670
Christmas... with the Doctor?

00:03:29.070 --> 00:03:31.640
Looks like it's going to be a lively Christmas Eve this year.

00:03:32.740 --> 00:03:35.910
Thank you, Doctor... Boss!

00:03:41.410 --> 00:03:43.910
There you go.
- Thank you.

00:03:44.940 --> 00:03:46.660
Hm? What?

00:03:46.690 --> 00:03:47.900
The tip of your nose.

00:03:49.690 --> 00:03:51.790
I'll put something on it.

00:03:56.070 --> 00:03:59.580
No, it's okay...
- Buck up.

00:04:21.900 --> 00:04:26.460
<i>And so their fun Christmas vacation began.</i>

00:04:27.660 --> 00:04:32.210
<i>All the boys came running to visit when they heard about it.</i>

00:04:34.650 --> 00:04:37.020
Wow, how pretty!

00:04:37.640 --> 00:04:41.460
Say, Romeo... That's the second thing you've hidden from us.

00:04:41.750 --> 00:04:43.050
What do you mean?

00:04:43.060 --> 00:04:46.460
First: that you don't have to work.

00:04:46.610 --> 00:04:47.810
And second?

00:04:48.500 --> 00:04:51.290
Second that you get to be with Bianca all the time.

00:04:52.340 --> 00:04:55.030
Hey, he's turning red!
- Bingo.

00:04:55.860 --> 00:04:57.030
Dante!

00:04:57.600 --> 00:04:58.370
Whoops...

00:04:59.620 --> 00:05:02.480
Wow, you're reading this book, Romeo?

00:05:02.490 --> 00:05:03.220
Yeah.

00:05:03.360 --> 00:05:07.730
He's so good. He's vowed to read two whole books during the vacation.

00:05:08.100 --> 00:05:10.670
Two books!
- Just amazing.

00:05:11.060 --> 00:05:13.500
Well... I AM the leader, after all.

00:05:14.000 --> 00:05:16.050
Then I'll get the second book.

00:05:16.090 --> 00:05:18.370
You're finished with the Three Little Pigs now, right?

00:05:19.320 --> 00:05:20.850
The Three...

00:05:20.880 --> 00:05:23.470
...Little Pigs?
- Gimme that!

00:05:26.620 --> 00:05:29.010
Three Little Pigs.
Oink, oink.

00:05:29.030 --> 00:05:31.970
Oink! Oink! Oink!

00:05:32.250 --> 00:05:38.730
Now I want to read a more difficult book.

00:05:39.330 --> 00:05:41.400
All right. I'll go look for one.

00:05:44.300 --> 00:05:46.650
Are you picking out books for Romeo?

00:05:46.670 --> 00:05:49.180
Yes. This is the perfect chance.

00:05:49.210 --> 00:05:53.990
I've wanted to teach the boy more ever since I taught him how to read.

00:05:54.780 --> 00:05:58.540
This is a good book... but a little too difficult for Romeo.

00:06:02.960 --> 00:06:08.370
Oh, my brother loved this book! How nostalgic!

00:06:08.540 --> 00:06:10.800
Doctor, I'm taking this for Romeo, okay?

00:06:13.980 --> 00:06:15.890
Moby... Dick?

00:06:16.190 --> 00:06:21.450
It's about a big, white MONSTER whale that no one could catch!

00:06:21.940 --> 00:06:24.910
Captain Ahab risks his life to catch him.

00:06:25.370 --> 00:06:28.490
Hmmm! Sounds interesting.

00:06:28.570 --> 00:06:33.490
Big Brother excitedly read it to me night after night...

00:06:33.940 --> 00:06:36.910
Alfredo liked it that much?

00:06:44.950 --> 00:06:47.720
All right then, I'll give it a shot!

00:06:55.640 --> 00:06:57.650
Gee... So many words I don't know...

00:06:58.760 --> 00:07:01.770
And the print is so tiny...

00:07:12.250 --> 00:07:17.160
<i>Can't fall asleep. Alfredo loved this book. Got to read it.</i>

00:07:17.690 --> 00:07:27.530
The sea became... tumul... tuous, and the men grew... courageous.

00:07:28.060 --> 00:07:33.550
<i>The sea became tumultuous, and the men grew courageous.</i>

00:07:41.200 --> 00:07:43.530
There she breaches! Moby Dick!

00:07:45.520 --> 00:07:49.040
Loose your harpoons!

00:08:07.220 --> 00:08:10.770
<i>Amazing... this is amazing, Alfredo!</i>

00:08:15.550 --> 00:08:16.610
Come in.

00:08:18.540 --> 00:08:22.850
Little nurse, there's a letter for you.
- Thank you.

00:08:26.720 --> 00:08:28.770
Another letter from your aunt?

00:08:29.740 --> 00:08:33.370
She's probably writing to ask me to come back home again.

00:08:36.500 --> 00:08:39.320
I'm sorry. I'm still confused...

00:08:39.380 --> 00:08:42.700
My aunt is a very nice person, you know...

00:08:44.500 --> 00:08:45.970
No rush.

00:08:46.900 --> 00:08:50.030
I think of you as my own daughter.

00:08:50.190 --> 00:08:51.960
You can stay here as long as you want.

00:08:53.350 --> 00:08:54.610
Dr. Casella...

00:08:55.750 --> 00:09:00.480
The important thing is to decide which would make you happiest...

00:09:00.530 --> 00:09:03.770
Going back home to live with your relatives...

00:09:03.790 --> 00:09:07.100
...or staying and growing up here.

00:09:07.200 --> 00:09:09.650
Let's take our time deciding.

00:09:11.570 --> 00:09:13.960
Well then, I'll go check in on...

00:09:14.410 --> 00:09:15.000
Yes...

00:09:15.720 --> 00:09:18.340
Bianca's patient.

00:09:27.620 --> 00:09:29.780
A big wave...! Ow.

00:09:35.050 --> 00:09:41.410
<i>Dr. Casella was delighted to see Romeo's singular dedication to reading.</i>

00:09:41.540 --> 00:09:49.240
<i>...now that he was not obliged to work ten hours a day. It gave him an idea.</i>

00:09:50.750 --> 00:09:51.440
What?

00:09:51.850 --> 00:09:54.410
In your grandfather's research laboratory?

00:09:55.300 --> 00:09:58.920
Dr. Casella says his grandfather was a university professor.

00:09:59.700 --> 00:10:02.900
He was a scholar of antiquities, and a naturalist as well.

00:10:03.740 --> 00:10:05.370
Antiquities?

00:10:05.740 --> 00:10:07.830
He must have been very important.

00:10:11.080 --> 00:10:16.470
It's been ages. I loved this room when I was a child.

00:10:30.030 --> 00:10:31.570
Are those...
- Bones?

00:10:31.650 --> 00:10:33.130
Of what?

00:10:33.450 --> 00:10:36.380
There's one in the book you're reading now, Romeo.

00:10:36.390 --> 00:10:37.830
A whale?

00:10:37.960 --> 00:10:42.370
This one is a Pygmy Right Whale.
One of the smaller whales.

00:10:42.950 --> 00:10:47.250
The legendary White Whale would have been ten times as big.

00:10:55.350 --> 00:10:56.290
Romeo.

00:10:58.500 --> 00:11:00.540
Look. This is the Earth.

00:11:00.660 --> 00:11:04.630
This is the Earth?
Where is Milan?

00:11:06.170 --> 00:11:08.650
Here.
- Milan's here?!

00:11:08.690 --> 00:11:12.370
Wow!
- Can we see more, doctor?

00:11:12.530 --> 00:11:15.910
Are you both interested in the things in this room?

00:11:15.950 --> 00:11:16.900
Yes!
- Yes!

00:11:17.380 --> 00:11:21.740
Very well. Starting today, this room will be your classroom.

00:11:21.850 --> 00:11:24.090
Our...
- classroom?

00:11:24.140 --> 00:11:25.320
Let's begin.

00:11:25.640 --> 00:11:28.530
Our first destination is the land of Geography.

00:11:37.690 --> 00:11:42.090
In order to set up trade with the East,

00:11:42.120 --> 00:11:44.590
...Vasco da Gama headed out on the open seas.

00:11:44.900 --> 00:11:47.890
Eventually, filled with hope, he rounded a certain cape.

00:11:48.510 --> 00:11:51.750
That was the Cape of Good Hope.
- The Cape of Good Hope...

00:11:53.790 --> 00:11:56.680
<i>Everything was a surprise to Romeo.</i>

00:11:57.000 --> 00:12:01.860
<i>Dr. Casella had brought him into the world of knowledge.</i>

00:12:02.420 --> 00:12:05.530
<i>Enchanted by the wonder that world had to offer, </i>

00:12:05.730 --> 00:12:07.300
<i>...Romeo took in everything with open eyes.</i>

00:12:08.780 --> 00:12:14.000
<i>Romeo enjoyed every moment he spent there.</i>

00:12:16.510 --> 00:12:20.010
A sperm whale, like the one Dr. Casella showed me.

00:12:22.820 --> 00:12:27.680
Humpback whale... Minke whale...

00:12:27.820 --> 00:12:29.680
White whale.

00:12:37.440 --> 00:12:41.350
All the things I've learned are spinning around in my head!

00:12:41.760 --> 00:12:44.030
Cities and oceans I never knew about!

00:12:45.080 --> 00:12:47.280
The world sure is big!

00:12:48.250 --> 00:12:49.730
That does it!

00:12:49.760 --> 00:12:52.760
I'm gonna keep studying, even when I go back to the boss's place.

00:12:52.800 --> 00:12:55.840
Here I come, world!

00:12:55.870 --> 00:12:58.360
In the middle of an adventure on the open seas?

00:12:59.100 --> 00:13:00.680
Ah... Yessir!

00:13:01.780 --> 00:13:05.680
Here's the star map you asked to see yesterday.

00:13:06.790 --> 00:13:09.680
The north star. Cassiopeia.

00:13:10.030 --> 00:13:12.330
The Big Bear... the Little Bear.

00:13:12.360 --> 00:13:14.550
Did you make this, Doctor?

00:13:15.420 --> 00:13:18.430
Well, I can't draw as well as Leonardo da Vinci, but...

00:13:26.870 --> 00:13:27.790
What's the matter?

00:13:28.100 --> 00:13:32.900
Doctor, why are you so kind to me?

00:13:33.420 --> 00:13:36.310
Because you have such great potential.

00:13:36.860 --> 00:13:40.590
It's a pleasure to watch it grow day by day.

00:13:42.150 --> 00:13:43.340
Want to take these with you?

00:13:43.450 --> 00:13:46.930
You can read them when you go back to your Padrone's home.

00:13:47.500 --> 00:13:48.020
Okay.

00:13:48.290 --> 00:13:51.290
I'm ready, Dr. Casella.

00:13:51.580 --> 00:13:54.270
All right then.
- You going somewhere, Bianca...?

00:13:57.380 --> 00:14:01.530
Every Saturday, the Doctor examines the children at the orphanage.

00:14:05.340 --> 00:14:07.990
Say "aah".

00:14:09.760 --> 00:14:13.890
Your cold is all gone now. All right.

00:14:17.580 --> 00:14:21.950
Now, now... Why the long face?

00:14:24.020 --> 00:14:26.280
It hurts here, Doctor.

00:14:26.670 --> 00:14:28.040
Let's see...

00:14:30.290 --> 00:14:32.320
There, all better now.

00:14:32.510 --> 00:14:38.560
Let's put a bandage over it, okay?
- Thank you very much.

00:14:39.750 --> 00:14:42.130
Look! Isn't it pretty?

00:14:43.530 --> 00:14:45.300
D - u - c - k.

00:14:46.720 --> 00:14:48.760
Wow, you can read!

00:14:49.140 --> 00:14:53.850
Hush now! You're bothering the doctor.

00:14:55.020 --> 00:14:59.430
Doctors just don't do what Dr. Casella does.

00:14:59.500 --> 00:15:05.000
The world would be a better place if there were more like him.

00:15:07.960 --> 00:15:10.450
Hey hey! I can't do my examinations.

00:15:19.730 --> 00:15:20.690
Come in.

00:15:21.400 --> 00:15:23.480
Bianca, where's Dr. Casella?

00:15:23.830 --> 00:15:25.550
House call.

00:15:27.740 --> 00:15:29.370
On Christmas Eve??

00:15:29.540 --> 00:15:34.250
Yes. He says tending to those sick and in pain is much more important.

00:15:43.620 --> 00:15:46.180
Bianca...
- What?

00:15:46.880 --> 00:15:50.680
What would I have become if I hadn't met Dr. Casella?

00:15:52.270 --> 00:15:54.210
I didn't know anything.

00:15:54.240 --> 00:15:57.440
If I hadn't met him, I wouldn't even be able to read.

00:16:00.820 --> 00:16:05.850
Me too. Dr. Casella tells me I'm like his own daughter.

00:16:15.500 --> 00:16:18.340
Romeo... it's like they said:

00:16:18.340 --> 00:16:23.540
The world would be a better place with more people like Dr. Casella.

00:16:24.280 --> 00:16:26.540
Children all over would be happy.

00:16:26.860 --> 00:16:27.800
Yeah.

00:16:30.100 --> 00:16:34.840
I wish I could tell him how grateful I am, but I can't figure out how to say it...

00:16:35.210 --> 00:16:36.810
Pathetic, isn't it?

00:16:38.190 --> 00:16:40.260
Grateful...

00:16:43.150 --> 00:16:44.010
That's it!

00:16:54.240 --> 00:16:57.830
Welcome back. The children have been waiting eagerly for you.

00:17:00.660 --> 00:17:03.570
Welcome back, Dr. Casella!

00:17:03.830 --> 00:17:05.910
Please be seated.

00:17:06.240 --> 00:17:08.380
What's in store for me...?

00:17:12.040 --> 00:17:15.550
Your Christmas present, Dr. Casella.

00:17:15.780 --> 00:17:17.450
Christmas present...?

00:17:17.740 --> 00:17:19.440
You have a seat too, Pia.

00:17:23.370 --> 00:17:26.170
We shall now put on a puppet show.

00:17:26.210 --> 00:17:31.160
Excuse our poor production, but this is a true story.

00:17:31.340 --> 00:17:32.190
Really?

00:17:32.640 --> 00:17:35.280
And so... begin!

00:17:37.740 --> 00:17:42.290
Long long ago there lived a boy and a girl.

00:17:43.790 --> 00:17:46.490
The boy was a chimney sweep.

00:17:47.020 --> 00:17:51.330
The girl was a sweet girl, though a bit of a tomboy.

00:17:51.330 --> 00:17:52.460
Tomboy?!

00:17:52.530 --> 00:17:54.450
That's mean, Romeo!

00:17:54.530 --> 00:17:57.810
Shh! Bianca, it's just a story!

00:17:57.840 --> 00:18:00.530
It's still a weird thing to say.

00:18:03.870 --> 00:18:06.870
There was a doctor they both liked very much.

00:18:07.070 --> 00:18:10.030
Get serious, Romeo!
- Oh, right.

00:18:12.720 --> 00:18:16.180
The doctor was very kind to the little girl.

00:18:16.200 --> 00:18:24.370
Why? Because she had lost her beloved brother and was all alone.

00:18:24.970 --> 00:18:30.370
The doctor lent a helping hand to lift the girl out of her sadness...

00:18:30.620 --> 00:18:34.690
And he said he would become her father.

00:18:45.890 --> 00:18:51.190
The girl was torn. She should have returned to her Martini family.

00:18:51.930 --> 00:18:58.170
But the longer she stayed with him, the stronger her feelings grew...

00:18:59.280 --> 00:19:01.370
The stronger her feelings...

00:19:07.410 --> 00:19:08.410
Bianca!

00:19:08.440 --> 00:19:10.300
The girl made a decision.

00:19:11.120 --> 00:19:18.890
She decided to not look back, and become a nurse to help the doctor.

00:19:20.190 --> 00:19:22.930
That's what she decided.

00:19:34.360 --> 00:19:39.620
The doctor also did many things for the boy.

00:19:40.170 --> 00:19:43.850
The boy wanted to do something to show his gratitude.

00:19:43.870 --> 00:19:47.450
But what can a little boy do...?

00:19:47.510 --> 00:19:51.100
Right then he heard his sister's voice saying...

00:19:52.420 --> 00:19:55.210
"If only there were more people like the doctor,

00:19:55.240 --> 00:19:57.640
...the world would be a happier place."

00:19:59.770 --> 00:20:01.570
The boy thought...

00:20:02.240 --> 00:20:05.380
If he became a person as great as the doctor when he grew up...

00:20:06.000 --> 00:20:13.270
He... no, I want to tell children about what the doctor did for me.

00:20:13.480 --> 00:20:15.400
That's my wish.

00:20:15.940 --> 00:20:16.650
Romeo...

00:20:23.010 --> 00:20:28.400
Dr. Casella... I don't know if I can...

00:20:28.490 --> 00:20:33.530
...but I want to keep studying and become a teacher!

00:20:35.170 --> 00:20:39.010
Of course you can, Romeo.
If anybody can, you can.

00:20:39.560 --> 00:20:44.570
Doctor. I'll do my very best!

00:20:51.750 --> 00:20:53.570
Will you let me stay here?

00:20:55.000 --> 00:20:58.320
I'm sure you'll become the best tomboy nurse in Milan.

00:21:01.890 --> 00:21:04.870
Congrats!
- Your doctor's great!

00:21:05.270 --> 00:21:08.370
I'm gonna study when I grow up, too!

00:21:19.100 --> 00:21:22.390
I've never had such a beautiful Christmas...

00:21:25.930 --> 00:21:32.390
<i>Alfredo... the world will be very different when we've grown up.</i>

00:21:33.290 --> 00:21:39.040
<i>Someday children will cry out in joy under this blue sky.</i>

00:21:39.460 --> 00:21:46.530
<i>I know... because everyone under the blue sky is free.</i>

00:21:55.100 --> 00:21:59.170
<i>Spring: time for the Black Brothers to return home.</i>

00:21:59.620 --> 00:22:02.760
<i>But also a day of sad farewells.</i>

00:22:03.520 --> 00:22:06.250
<i>We'll always be together...
no matter how far apart.</i>

00:22:07.700 --> 00:22:11.770
<i>Skyward! On Wings of Freedom!</i>

00:22:07.700 --> 00:22:11.770
Last episode:

00:22:13.130 --> 00:22:17.070
<i>"Si Si Ciao ~ On These Roman Roofs"</i>

00:22:25.540 --> 00:22:29.640
<i>Si Si Ciao, why do the good times</i>

00:22:29.740 --> 00:22:33.940
<i>seem to end so soon?</i>

00:22:34.140 --> 00:22:38.140
<i>Si Si Ciao, we're all friends</i>

00:22:38.340 --> 00:22:42.340
<i>Let's meet again on these Roman roofs</i>

00:22:42.950 --> 00:22:47.250
<i>Your laughing voice dances</i>

00:22:47.250 --> 00:22:51.150
<i>Once again in the sky</i>

00:22:51.550 --> 00:22:58.450
<i>Your pocket bursting with memories</i>

00:23:00.150 --> 00:23:04.050
<i>Si Si Ciao, goodbye but for now</i>

00:23:04.250 --> 00:23:08.250
<i>Let's meet again on these Roman roofs</i>
